# Codex execpolicy rules — canonical source; agent/scripts/sync-agent-config.sh
# links the containing rules/ directory to ~/.codex/rules.
#
# The file is Starlark, so `#` comments are real comments. Each prefix_rule()
# pre-approves a command whose leading tokens match `pattern`, so read-only and
# otherwise routine commands run without an approval prompt. Codex appends new
# entries here itself whenever the maintainer approves a command "always".
#
# Validate a single command against these rules with:
#   codex execpolicy check --rules ~/.dotfiles/agent/codex/rules/default.rules -- ls -la
# It prints the matched rule and the decision as JSON, and exits non-zero with a
# parse error if the file is malformed.

